<title>JAPAN: Japan buys 147,000 tonnes wheat, 20,000 barley.</title>
<headline>Japan buys 147,000 tonnes wheat, 20,000 barley.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1996-09-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>Japan's Food Agency said on Thursday it had bought 80,000 tonnes of U.S. wheat, 50,000 of Canadian wheat and 20,000 of Canadian barley at its weekly tender, all for November shipment.</p>
<p>It also bought 17,000 tonnes of Australian wheat for October shipment.</p>
<p>The tender results details were as follows, in tonnes: WHEAT  Country    Quantity	 Type</p>
<p> U.S.	 80,000	   Western white	    20,000</p>
<p>				   Dark northern spring   36,000</p>
<p>				   Hard red winter</p>
<p>				    (11.5 percent protein) 4,000</p>
<p>				    (13 percent protein)  20,000</p>
<p> Canada     50,000	   1 Canadian western red spring</p>
<p> Australia  17,000	   Prime Hard (October shipment)</p>
<p>BARLEY  Canada     20,000	   Feed			 20,000</p>
</text>
